                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "\"Kim Jong-Boom is a game in which Kim confronts Donald through the arcade game\".\nOk Azimut Team, we got it, this is a game.\nFor 100 megabytes and almost 2$, we get some kind of stupid meme-related memory game.. I kind of hate all these games who live on memes or just on the present times - we have Trump and Kim (yeah, that's his surname by the way) and so let's make games about them, when we'll have other politicians let's make games on them and so on.. did we forget all the games that came out about tyde pods, uganda, fidget spinners..\nThis is a simple game of match the cards - you'll play for the United States or North Korea and you'll have to.. match the cards, covered by a nuclear red and yellow sign.\nAnd the game has also some bugs, I had a hard time just to boot it up but also the skirmish mode won't work for anyone, as far as I have read and heard.\nApart from that, the game has just a timer and you'll have to match stupidly-designed minimalistic cards.. some of them are just two or three lines, others depict stars or similar symbols.\nThe whole game is extremely repetitive and if this wasn't enough, the game resets all your progress so that you're forced to do everything in one session if you want all the achievements.\nIt's just a memory game, pair two cards before the slow timer runs out. Nothing more.\nObviously, this game will never have trading cards even if the Steam store page claims the contrary.\nHave fun starting every single time at 0-0 even if you've played already 40 matches of the same stupid memory matching thing..",
